Welcome!

This is a **{{ node_type }} node** in a self-hosted Kubernetes cluster configured via [this-oliver/homelab](https://github.com/this-oliver/homelab).

## General

{% if node_type == 'controller' %}
Kubernetes (MicroK8s):

- Version: `{{ k8s_version }}`
- Kubeconfig: {{ base_summary_kubeconfig }}
- Worker Nodes: {{ workers | length }}

{% if nodes %}
Nodes:
{% for node in nodes -%}
- `{{ node.name }}` (k8s {{ node.version }}) - { role: {{ node.role }}, address: {{ node.address }}, ready: {{ ready_labels.get(node.ready, node.ready) }} }
{% endfor %}
{% else %}
No nodes reported. The cluster is not running, or the kubeconfig at {{ base_summary_kubeconfig }} is not readable.
{% endif %}

## Access

Services:

- Headlamp dashboard ({{ headlamp.get('version', '') or 'version not detected' }}): {{ headlamp_url }}
- Traefik dashboard ({{ traefik.get('version', '') or 'version not detected' }}): {{ traefik_url }}
- TLS configured:

Good to know:
- Headlamp uses RBAC - create a token with `kubectl create token headlamp-admin -n kube-system`
- Traefik dashboard sits behind basic auth — sign in as `{{ homelab.admin.username }}`.
- The only public entry point is HAProxy on ports `80` and `443`. Everything behind it lives on NodePorts that are firewalled to loopback.

